  "details": "I suggest to count number of curves/keyframes used in player's custom animations.\nThat's because in VRC, movements of Player's avatars mostly controlled by IK retargeting than by fixed baked animations for NPC characters, that means very detailed movements in animations is not necessary and can be significantly simplified w/o noticeble visual changes. High ammount of curves/keyframes noticeble increases memory usage and also CPU usage.\n\nIt's popular to use Mixamo animations or MMD dances, but most creators don't adjust export/import settings, so animations got added into avatars as-is almost raw. This can motivate creators to work more deeply on animations.",
